cvcpkg: run scripts in LuaJIT when lupa has no Lua 5.1 module.

fakeredis runs EVAL/EVALSHA/FCALL in lupa.lua51 unless FAKEREDIS_LUA_VERSION
names another of lupa.lua51..lua54. lupa's PyPI wheels compile all of those
in, but cvcpkg's lupa-cpXY columns link cvcpkg's own Lua 5.4 and LuaJIT 2.1
and ship only lupa.lua54 and lupa.luajit21. Without this the import fails,
fakeredis drops its scripting commands without a word, and every EVAL answers
"unknown command 'eval'".

Lua 5.4 is no substitute: Redis scripts are Lua 5.1 (global unpack, no
integer subtype). LuaJIT 2.1 is the 5.1 dialect, so the default version
falls back to lupa.luajit21. An explicit FAKEREDIS_LUA_VERSION still fails
loudly when its module is missing.

--- a/fakeredis/commands_mixins/scripting_mixin.py
+++ b/fakeredis/commands_mixins/scripting_mixin.py
@@ -32,7 +32,14 @@
 LUA_VERSION = os.getenv("FAKEREDIS_LUA_VERSION", "5.1")
 
 with lupa.allow_lua_module_loading():
-    LUA_MODULE = importlib.import_module(__LUA_RUNTIMES_MAP[LUA_VERSION])
+    try:
+        LUA_MODULE = importlib.import_module(__LUA_RUNTIMES_MAP[LUA_VERSION])
+    except ImportError:
+        # cvcpkg's lupa has no lupa.lua51 (see the patch header): use LuaJIT,
+        # the Lua 5.1 dialect that Redis and Valkey run scripts in.
+        if LUA_VERSION != "5.1":
+            raise
+        LUA_MODULE = importlib.import_module("lupa.luajit21")
 
 LOGGER = logging.getLogger("fakeredis")
 REDIS_LOG_LEVELS = {
